<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Saving the Third Temple, 1973</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY text=#dcdcdc bgColor=#2b2b2b scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Saving the Third Temple, 1973&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al “Beirutdude” Sandrik&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;The Time Is: 8 October 1973, 03:00 Zulu/05:00 Golan Heights Time&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Designed: September 2021 C:MO V1.03 Build 1174.30&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Eastern Mediterranean Sea/Israel/Golan Heights&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Playable as USN only&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Duration: 13 Hours&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;This is an alternative history scenario&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Background: &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;On the morning of October 6th, 1973 Israeli military intelligence announced to Golda Meir’s “Kitchen Cabinet” that war would begin that evening with simultaneous attacks on both the Sinai and Golan Fronts. A preemptive air strike was considered and rejected as the Israeli Cabinet wanted it clear the Arabs had struck first. After consultation with the American government, USN Carrier Task Force (CTF) 60.1 led by the USS Independence (CV-62) and the Amphibious Ready Group (ARG) led by the USS Guadalcanal (LPH-7 - not modeled in the scenario) were dispatched at high speed from their positions southeast of Crete toward Israel in case they were needed for a Non-combatant Evacuation Operation (NEO). &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;At 14:05 Israeli Time the Egyptians struck crossing the Suez Canal in swarms of rubber boats and the Syrians threw multiple armored columns toward the Golan. &lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;The Israeli Air Force (IAF) quickly swung into action launching Close Air Support (CAS) attacks on both fronts, and in both cases, they were shocked as swarms of SA-2, 3, 6, and 7 SAMs rose to meet their aircraft scoring multiple hits. Further the plentiful ZSU-23-4 Shilka and older ZSU-57-2 Ob'yekt 500 SPAA vehicles threw up curtains of steel making low level attacks almost suicidal. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;During that afternoon and night Israeli Defense Forces (IDF) ground troops fought a despite holding action on the Golan, but seeing the IAF aircraft losses they made a deliberate decision to not call for CAS. Despite that on the 7th IAF pilots attempted to intervene with similar results. That morning, Prime Minister Golda Meir was in touch with American Secretary of State Henry Kissinger pleading for American resupply of aircraft, tanks and antitank weapons. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;During the Afternoon of the 7th the Syrian first Armored Division reached the escarpment along the road to the Gesher Benot Yaakov (Benot Ya’akov Bridge) crossing the River Jordan into northern Galilee. Seeing an opportunity, the Syrian commander pushed recon and armored elements down the valley and across the bridge taking up defensive positions within Israel itself while awaiting the rest of the 1st Armored to move forward. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;The IAF response was furious launching “Operation Model 5” to clear the Syrian SAM belts and allow strike aircraft to attack the Syrian columns moving toward the bridge. It was a costly failure! IAF A-4s, Mirages and Phantom II’s fell prey to the SA-6s/7s and Shilkas placed along either side of the road. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;By nightfall only a thin band of tanks from the IDF 679th Reserve Armored Brigade and paratroopers took up blocking positions on the heights above the Jordan Valley, but optimism that the Syrians could be stopped was waning. Moshe Dayan visited Major General Hofi’s headquarters in Nafah, Golan Heights and was shocked at the sense of doom and hopelessness that pervaded the command. He returned to Tel Aviv and walked into the Cabinet meeting exclaiming, “Golda, all is lost! We can’t hold them! This is the end of the Third Temple! We must invoke the Sampson Option to save what we can before it is too late!” &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;After a fiery meeting Golda Meir calmed her jittery Defense Minister affirming, she would call the United States and see what could be done, but no one would use nuclear weapons until it was absolutely necessary. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;After many years the transcript of the call that led to the historic events of the 8th has been released…&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;“Henry, this is Golda. Moshe has just come back from the Golan; Syrian tanks are currently in the Jordan River Valley and that has been confirmed by our Intelligence agencies. We don’t know if we can hold them and he wants to use nukes on the spearheads.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Golda, you can’t be serious!&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Henry, we have taken massive losses. A simple resupply of aircraft, tanks and weapons just isn’t enough anymore. Without more substantial support we will have no choice. We are going to launch air strikes on Syrian Air Force bases tomorrow and counter attack in the Sinai. If neither are successful, we may have no other option!&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Golda, the USS Independence will be arriving west of Haifa overnight. I can get you one day of air strikes but only against Syrian units in the Golan and Jordan Valley. We can’t be seen to be attacking into Syria itself or doing more than stabilizing the situation. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;You can promise this without President Nixon’s commitment? &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;He is so caught up in Watergate, and his drinking, right now he will take me at my word. Given the seriousness of the situation, I can get this done. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Henry, I have got to show results to my people. If things go badly tomorrow, I fear we will have to invoke the Sampson Option late in the afternoon or by evening. We will make sure the world knows your aircraft are not over Syria proper. This is dangerous, I don’t know how the Soviets will react, but I fear there are just no other options!&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Golda, just remember I can get you a day, but after that, I can guarantee nothing. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;I understand Henry, I will make arrangements on our end. This has to work or God help us all! God be with you Henry; Moshe will call your Secretary of Defense to work out the details”&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Transcript ends&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Notes:&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Please ensure your Pop-Up Messages are activated, there could be a few messages.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT color=#ffffff face=Calibri&gt;For some reason my game interface opens up on the USS Little Rock and I can't get it to center on any other unit. Just click on CTF 60.1 to see the Independence CVBG.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Check the WRA for your loadputs to make sure it is set the way &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;YOU&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; want it set&lt;/STRONG&gt;. Because of the nature of the airstrikes I have adjusted the WRA to drop 1 or 2 "dumb bombs" from 1 or 2 aircraft depending upon the target. For example a soft mobile target may&amp;nbsp;be allocated&amp;nbsp;1 weapon each from&amp;nbsp;2 aircraft where a hard mobile target my be allocated 2 weapons each from 2 aircraft. &lt;STRONG&gt;So check your WRA!!!!!!!&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;I spent a week ELIMINATING units to increase scenario speed and performance!!!!!! Please consider that before you recommend the cool unit you think really should be in the scenario (SR-71 anyone?)!!!!! On fast (fire symbol) speed the scenario should now take 3 to 4 hours of real time to play as opposed to the 12-13 hours it took during my initial play tests.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;As there are variable entry probabilities for USSR submarine units, IF you like to play in the Scenario Editor, you MUST start the game with the “Start New Game” button, then save it. Then you can open the save file in the Scenario Editor. Otherwise, ALL submarine units will appear (even those with a 25% chance of appearing!!!!!) in the scenario and you might not like that!!!!!&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;The Soviets have a few submarines near you. They are entirely dependent upon variable entry, so no one knows how many and what type. That should keep your ASW/Submarine assets busy and maybe allow for some changes for replay. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;A/I units and the USN Submarines teleport at 03:00:05 UTC, so please let the USN SSN OPAREA ASW mission go for at least 10 seconds until the teleport happens. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;I set up some USN missions, delete them if you prefer. They’re just housekeeping stuff like SSN ASW/AEW/AAW-CAP/ASW and Tanker missions. I just set them up to het things going, otherwisethe airstrike missions are yours to set and reset what you like &lt;STRONG&gt;after teleporting&lt;/STRONG&gt;. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;I did choose loadouts for the aircraft as the scenario still plays a bit slow. I suggest you change loadouts in the Scenario Editor if you don’t like my choices. Personally, I don’t care if you change them, just have fun. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;The USSR and USN start mutually “Unfriendly” to each other.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Israel and the USN are mutually “Friendly.”.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Syria and the USN/Israel are mutually “Hostile” to each other respectively.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Syria and the USSR are mutually “Neutral” to each other (this is to help avoid the USSR jumping in when Syrian units are destroyed). In reality they are “Friendly” but let’s see how this plays out…&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;There are “Friendly” geographic aimpoints in Syrian held territory, they are supposed to be like that (trust me)! You need not worry about them and you definitely should not attack them. They will serve their purpose if things go badly in the scenario (USN Score less than&amp;nbsp;999 around 13:00:00 utc). DO NOT mark them as “Hostile” or BAD THINGS could happen earlier (again, trust me). I can see you all doing it now!!!! I really suggest you suppress the desire and play the scenario out to its conclusion first.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Fog of War (FoG): In high tension situations with people's nerves on edge, BAD THINGS can happen. Lookouts (especially 17 and 18 year old Boatswain's Mates on watch) misinterpet what they are seeing, Junior Officers get jittery, the media releases erronerous reports, HUMINT passes on bad information, etc. All of that can lead to a big mistake being made, don't be suprised if it happens.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;While you are allied with Israel, the IAF units are actually doing their own thing waging an air campaign against Syrian airfields and conducting AAW/CAP over Galilee. The IDF ground units will engage the Syrians and yes, the IAF Aircraft/IDF ground unit losses count against your score. Your job is to ease Israeli fears about being overrun and drawing their leadership back from the “Sampson (Nuclear) Option.” If the IDF is doing poorly that isn’t happening and Moshe Dayan is getting more nervous, this may have consequences late in the scenario.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;I suggest you play this one to the end, even if your airstrikes have concluded. It does play a little slow at times because of all the ground units but you might want to finish it, just saying. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;All airfields are single unit airports (to save on units and help improve game performance). No airfield should be CONVENTIONALLY attacked by you (you shouldn’t be able to). Should, by some chance, you receive nuclear release each airbase has a geographic aimpoint for you to use to attack them. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;You may not attack into Syria or Jordan, that is the IAF Operations Area and National Command Authority (actually Henry Kissinger) has explicitly ordered you to stay out of post 1967 Syrian and Jordanian territory. If you are granted nuclear release, that No Navigation Zone will be removed.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;There was a late issue with the USS Independence CVBG. Without getting into details, the carrier was accidently deleted and had to be rebuilt. To give it a forward speed at the scenario start would entail massive work, so it starts out at dead stop but is set to gain 20 knots quickly. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Scoring: Disaster = 0000 and Triumph = 1,500&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;A Delta INI file is included with the Zip File for rebuilds &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN'&gt;Originally created: Command: Modern Operations (C:MO) &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;C:MO V1.03 Build 1174.30&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Updated: TBD&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al “BeirutDude” Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN'&gt;&lt;FONT color=white face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin'&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
